From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jassim Shanavaskhan <jshanava@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Tue, 09 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: fix silent channel change failure after hostapd SIGHUP

Problem:
- WiFi.Radio.X.Channel=Y is silently dropped with "disconnected, no
  applying of chanspec" after SSID enable on a non-last radio
- wpa_ctrl managers of all previously-enabled radios remain permanently
  disconnected after the SIGHUP issued by wifiGen_hapd_reloadDaemon()

Cause:
- wld_secDmn_reconnectGrpMgrs() is called synchronously after kill(),
  before CTRL-EVENT-TERMINATING is delivered; connect() exits early with
  "already connected" since isConnected() still returns true at that
  point; when TERMINATING later arrives and sets isReady=false, no
  reconnect timer is running
- checkAllIfaces() calls setConnectionInfo() on sockets belonging to
  sibling managers, issuing DETACH and creating an infinite reconnect
  loop every 500 ms

Fix:
- move wld_wpaCtrlMngr_connect() into s_ifaceTerminatingEvt() so it
  fires after isReady is already false, correctly arming the reconnect
  timer for every manager that receives TERMINATING
- guard setConnectionInfo() in checkAllIfaces() with (pCurrMgr == pMgr)
  to prevent managers from interfering with sibling connections
- retain wld_secDmn_reconnectGrpMgrs() calls at reload sites as a
  secondary path for managers already disconnected before the SIGHUP
- add GEN_FSM_STOP_HOSTAPD + GEN_FSM_START_HOSTAPD fallback in
  wifiGen_rad_setChanspec() if wpa_ctrl is still dead at channel-change
  time

Signed-off-by: Jassim Shanavaskhan <jshanava@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
--- a/src/nl80211/wld_secDmn.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_secDmn.c
@@ -243,6 +243,21 @@
     return SWL_RC_OK;
 }
 
+void wld_secDmn_reconnectGrpMgrs(wld_secDmn_t* pSecDmn) {
+    ASSERTS_NOT_NULL(pSecDmn, , ME, "NULL");
+    if(!wld_secDmn_isGrpMember(pSecDmn)) {
+        wld_wpaCtrlMngr_connect(pSecDmn->wpaCtrlMngr);
+        return;
+    }
+    uint32_t nMbr = wld_secDmnGrp_getMembersCount(pSecDmn->secDmnGroup);
+    for(uint32_t i = 0; i < nMbr; i++) {
+        wld_secDmn_t* pMbr = (wld_secDmn_t*) wld_secDmnGrp_getMemberByPos(pSecDmn->secDmnGroup, i);
+        if(pMbr != NULL) {
+            wld_wpaCtrlMngr_connect(pMbr->wpaCtrlMngr);
+        }
+    }
+}
+
 swl_rc_ne wld_secDmn_restart(wld_secDmn_t* pSecDmn) {
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pSecDmn, SWL_RC_INVALID_PARAM, ME, "NULL");
     ASSERT_NOT_NULL(pSecDmn->dmnProcess, SWL_RC_ERROR, ME, "NULL");
